.Dd June 26, 2026
.Dt CAP_LOOKUP_CAPMODE 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cap_lookup_capmode
.Nd require capability mode for directory fd lookups
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/capsicum.h
.Ft int
.Fn cap_lookup_capmode "int fd"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn cap_lookup_capmode
system call sets a monotonic per-descriptor flag that requires the
calling process to be in capability mode
.Pq see Xr cap_enter 2
before the directory descriptor may be used as the
.Fa dirfd
argument to any
.Xr \&*at 2
system call (such as
.Xr openat 2 ,
.Xr connectat 2 ,
.Xr fstatat 2 ,
etc.).
.Pp
Once set, any attempt to use the descriptor for path lookups from a
process not in capability mode will fail with
.Er ENOTCAPABLE .
.Pp
The flag is monotonic: once set it cannot be cleared.
Calling
.Fn cap_lookup_capmode
on a descriptor that already has the flag set is permitted and has no
effect.
.Pp
This is typically used to restrict access to a directory that has been
pre-opened for use by a sandboxed worker.
The directory can be passed to the worker via
.Xr recvmsg 2
with
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS ,
and the flag ensures only capability-mode processes can traverse it.
.Pp
This system call is allowed in capability mode
.Pq see Xr cap_enter 2 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn cap_lookup_capmode
succeeds unless:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBADF
The
.Fa fd
argument is not a valid active descriptor.
.It Bq Er ENOSYS
The running kernel was compiled without
.Cd "options CAPABILITIES" .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cap_enter 2 ,
.Xr cap_xfer_capmode 2 ,
.Xr openat 2 ,
.Xr capsicum 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn cap_lookup_capmode
system call first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
